              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Neal K. Katyal), eleven times Congress explicitly said there is no automatic stay during interlocutory appeals, including the day before Section\u202f16(a) was enacted."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Neal K. Katyal)",
